efore you see it."},{"id":"6-5-2","place":"the floor of the round room","actions":[{"attr":"Craft","verb":"gather up what lies on the floor"},{"attr":"Intellect","verb":"read the scratches by daylight"}],"clueTitle":"Sums begun again","clueText":"On the floor lie the sky-watchers'' slates, scratched with long sums. Many are crossed through and begun again.","hintFor":2,"lateLine":"You go over the same ground twice before you see it."},{"id":"6-5-3","place":"where the rows stop","actions":[{"attr":"Might","verb":"climb the ledges to the last rows"},{"attr":"Craft","verb":"run a thumb along the last cuts"}],"clueTitle":"Cut in a hurry","clueText":"In the last rows before they stop, every moon is cut to the right depth, but the edges are rough, as if made in a hurry. Not one night is missing.","hintFor":1,"lateLine":"You go over the same ground twice before you see it."}],"meaningQuestion":"*\"Be there when it does.\"* Be there to do what?","weekQuestion":"What will the fifth do in his hall?","pull":"**You have the hour. One piece is left, and the Seekers'' way ends at a blank rock with this same moon beside it. Tomorrow is the last day.**"}'::jsonb),
