with the lamp"}],"clueTitle":"The swept fan","clueText":"At the foot of the blank rock, the old grit on your side lies swept flat in a smooth quarter-circle. Its point is at the rock''s left edge.","hintFor":2,"lateLine":"By the time you find it, the fire is the only light left."},{"id":"6-6-3","place":"the streets you crossed this morning","actions":[{"attr":"Aim","verb":"look back down the hill from the crack"},{"attr":"Agility","verb":"go back the long way, street by street"}],"clueTitle":"Every post empty","clueText":"The crossroads, the gate-tower, the street under the wall: every place where a soldier stood is empty now. Only the pale marks of their boots are left.","hintFor":1,"lateLine":"By the time you find it, the fire is the only light left."}],"meaningQuestion":"*\"Finish what we could not.\"* What did the Seekers leave unfinished?","weekQuestion":"What will the fifth do in his hall?","pull":"**Tomorrow night, when the moon goes dark: through the Seekers'' door, into his hall, with the fifth in your hands.**"}'::jsonb)
